  "category": "multi-file-feature",
  "objective": "Add two options to wordcount: --top N prints the N most common words after the total, and --ignore-case counts words case-insensitively.",
  "acceptance": [
    "Without options the output is unchanged: one line \"words: <total>\".",
    "--top N prints, after the total line, up to N lines \"<word> <count>\", most frequent first, with ties in ascending string order (Python's default sort order).",
    "--ignore-case lowercases words before counting, so the printed words are lowercase; the total is unchanged.",
    "--top must be a positive integer: 0, a negative number, or a non-number makes main exit with status 2 through argparse.",
